 "limitations": [
  "Each record says an organism was recorded at a place and time by someone, as a human observation, a preserved specimen, a fossil specimen, a machine observation or another basis; a fossil specimen records an organism of an earlier age, not a living one. It is not a measurement of presence or abundance: the same species can be common and unrecorded, or rare and recorded often.",
  "Records follow where people look. Roads, villages, trails, reserves and the habits of a few observers shape where records fall, and a quiet area is not an empty one.",
  "Years reflect recording effort. A rise or fall in records per year follows the arrival of observation apps, surveys and datasets, not the organisms, and the counts by year are not a trend.",
  "Coordinates are as recorded with their stated uncertainty, which is missing for some records and larger than the catchment for others; a kept record is inside the catchment polygon at its recorded point only.",
  "Only records under CC0 1.0 or CC BY 4.0 are kept; records under other licences were dropped and are counted, so the kept records are a part of what GBIF holds here. Each dataset is credited to its publisher.",
  "The request was made on a stated date; GBIF records are added, corrected and withdrawn over time, so a later request can give other counts.",
  "A zero for a named plant means no kept record under that name inside the catchment, not that the plant is absent, and names can be recorded under synonyms."
